---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import StatusPill from '../../../components/docs/StatusPill.astro'

const LINKS = {
  spec17: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako/blob/main/docs/spec/17-runtime-driver-contract.md',
  spec06: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako/blob/main/docs/spec/06-launcher-abi.md',
  layoutSchema: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako/blob/main/docs/spec/schemas/layout.yaml',
  driverCrate: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako/tree/main/crates/tebako-driver',
  rubyRepo: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/ruby',
  runtimeRepo: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako-runtime-ruby',
  runtimeReleases: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako-runtime-ruby/releases',
  dwarfsTRs: 'https://github.com/tamatebako/dwarfs-t-rs',
}
---
<!-- normative: spec 17, spec 06 -->

<DocsLayout
  section="architecture"
  href="/docs/architecture/runtime-as-image/"
  title="Runtime as image"
  heading="Runtime as image."
  description="A tebako runtime is two artifacts — the interpreter exe and the env .tfs image — co-mounted with your payloads in one process. TEBAKO_RUNTIME_IMAGE, the single-owner mount root, and the TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT override."
>
  <p slot="lede" class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
      A tebako runtime is not one binary. It is <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">two artifacts</strong> —
      an interpreter executable and an env <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-base">.tfs</code> image —
      downloaded once, sha256-verified, and <em>mounted</em> — never extracted — into the same
      process as the payloads it runs.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] px-5 py-4" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
      <StatusPill status="shipped" note="spec 17 · crates/tebako-driver" />
      <span class="text-sm text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">the Rust driver mounts the env image + payload images in one process; contract-2 runtimes ship from the runtime factory</span>
      <StatusPill status="planned" note="windows exec/lock parity — roadmap 02" />
      <span class="text-sm text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">the handoff is shipped on macOS/Linux; the windows exec and locking port is still landing (spec 06 status)</span>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ WHY TWO ARTIFACTS ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">Why the runtime is two artifacts.</h2>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        The interpreter changes on the ruby release line; the files it runs against — stdlib,
        gems, its own layout declaration — change with it, but they are <em>content</em>, and
        content wants different treatment than a process entry point. Splitting the pair buys
        four things:
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">SHARE</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The pair is downloaded once per machine into the shared cache and reused by every
            package that names it — never duplicated into each package's bytes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">VERIFY</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The image is a first-class content object with its own sha256 trust anchor, verified
            at install and re-verified only on re-fetch — <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">never per run</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">MOUNT, DON'T EXTRACT</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The cache holds immutable artifacts only — no extracted layout tree. At run time the
            driver mounts the image whole; nothing materializes a mutable copy of an immutable
            artifact.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">RELEASE INDEPENDENTLY</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The runtime factory publishes the pair per version × platform triplet, with its own
            manifest and checksums. The product consumes the published release — it never
            rebuilds a runtime.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ THE TWO ARTIFACTS ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h2>Two artifacts, one runtime.</h2>
        <StatusPill status="shipped" note="dual-published since the image era" />
      </div>
      <p class="mb-6 max-w-2xl text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        Every image-era release of{' '}
        <a href={LINKS.runtimeReleases} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">tebako-runtime-ruby</a>
        {' '}publishes the pair plus a machine index (<code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">manifest.json</code>,
        carrying an <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">image</code> key and the{' '}
        <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">contract_version</code>) and SHA256SUMS:
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">A · THE INTERPRETER</p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">tebako-runtime-&lt;ver&gt;-&lt;ruby&gt;-&lt;triplet&gt;[.exe]</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The process entry point, statically linked against the Rust runtime driver (
            <a href={LINKS.driverCrate} class="tb-link-underline text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">crates/tebako-driver</a>
            — the v1 C++ <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">tebako-main.cpp</code> is
            retired). At exec it is handed the path of its env image and mounts it instead of
            any embedded image.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">B · THE ENV IMAGE</p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">tebako-runtime-&lt;ver&gt;-&lt;ruby&gt;-&lt;triplet&gt;.tfs</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The runtime's files — <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">lib/ruby</code>,
            gems, everything the interpreter's load paths expect — plus the pair declaration{' '}
            <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">/lib/tebako/layout.yaml</code>.
            Installed read-only (0444), mounted whole at the runtime root.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ DIAGRAM: THE PAIR, THE HANDOFF, THE BOOT ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">The pair, the handoff, the boot.</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 max-w-3xl text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        The exact wire grammar is the runtime driver contract,{' '}
        <a href={LINKS.spec17} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">spec 17</a>;
        the loader's side of it is{' '}
        <a href={LINKS.spec06} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">spec 06</a>.
        From cache entry to running interpreter:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 940 460" class="w-full min-w-[760px]" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="From cache to boot: the cache entry holds the interpreter and the env image; the loader exports TEBAKO_RUNTIME_IMAGE and execs the interpreter with image triples and an entry; the driver mounts the env image whole at the runtime root, verifies the pair, mounts payloads, installs the jail, rewrites argv">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ri-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <!-- panel A: the cache entry -->
          <g transform="translate(20, 20)">
            <rect width="270" height="340" rx="14" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="135" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">THE CACHE ENTRY — ~/.tebako</text>
            <text x="135" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">runtimes/ruby-3.3.7-0.16.0-macos-arm64/</text>

            <rect x="20" y="70" width="230" height="58" rx="8" fill="var(--color-ink)" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="135" y="94" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-mist-pale)">the interpreter</text>
            <text x="135" y="112" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--color-mist)" opacity="0.85">tebako-runtime-…  · 0755</text>

            <rect x="20" y="140" width="230" height="58" rx="8" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="135" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-paper)">the env image</text>
            <text x="135" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--color-paper)" opacity="0.9">tebako-runtime-….tfs · 0444</text>

            <g font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">
              <text x="30" y="222">sha256 / origin — exe markers</text>
              <text x="30" y="242">.tfs.sha256 — the trust anchor:</text>
              <text x="30" y="258">verified at install, never per run</text>
              <text x="30" y="278">.tfs.origin — the fetch URL</text>
            </g>
            <text x="135" y="316" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">artifacts only — no extracted tree</text>
          </g>

          <line x1="296" y1="190" x2="322" y2="190" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ri-arrow)" />

          <!-- panel B: the handoff -->
          <g transform="translate(328, 20)">
            <rect width="270" height="340" rx="14" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="135" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">THE HANDOFF — exec</text>
            <text x="135" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">bootstrap · the shim · tebako run</text>

            <g font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9.5">
              <text x="20" y="84" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">env</text>
              <rect x="20" y="94" width="230" height="30" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.2" />
              <text x="135" y="113" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)" font-size="8.5">TEBAKO_RUNTIME_IMAGE=&lt;cached .tfs&gt;</text>
              <text x="20" y="146" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">argv</text>
              <text x="28" y="168" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">--tebako-image</text>
              <text x="28" y="184" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">&#160;&#160;&lt;self|path&gt;:&lt;slot|-&gt;:&lt;mount&gt; …</text>
              <text x="28" y="206" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">--tebako-entry &lt;argv0&gt; &lt;args…&gt;</text>
              <text x="20" y="240" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">policy</text>
              <text x="28" y="260" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">TEBAKO_JAIL / TEBAKO_JAIL_SOURCE</text>
            </g>
            <text x="135" y="300" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">never returns on success —</text>
            <text x="135" y="316" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">the process becomes the runtime</text>
          </g>

          <line x1="604" y1="190" x2="630" y2="190" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ri-arrow)" />

          <!-- panel C: the boot -->
          <g transform="translate(636, 20)">
            <rect width="284" height="340" rx="14" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="142" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">THE BOOT — ONE PROCESS</text>

            <g font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-2)">
              <text x="24" y="62"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">1</tspan>&#160;&#160;validate TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT's form</text>
              <text x="46" y="78" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">malformed → exit 65, naming the variable</text>

              <text x="24" y="108"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">2</tspan>&#160;&#160;mount the env image WHOLE at the</text>
              <text x="46" y="124">runtime root — /__tfs__ (A:/t on windows)</text>

              <text x="24" y="154"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">3</tspan>&#160;&#160;verify the pair: layout.yaml vs the exe</text>
              <text x="46" y="170" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">mismatch → exit 78, before any payload</text>

              <text x="24" y="200"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">4</tspan>&#160;&#160;mount payload triples in argv order</text>
              <text x="46" y="216" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">exclusive onto occupied → EEXIST, by name</text>

              <text x="24" y="246"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">5</tspan>&#160;&#160;install the jail — after the mounts</text>
              <text x="46" y="262" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">malformed TEBAKO_JAIL → exit 73</text>

              <text x="24" y="292"><tspan font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)">6</tspan>&#160;&#160;rewrite argv to the entry; the</text>
              <text x="46" y="308">interpreter starts</text>
            </g>
          </g>

          <text x="470" y="400" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">Any failure along the way unmounts everything — never a partial mount. The env image is mounted, never extracted;</text>
          <text x="470" y="418" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">the mount table is longest-prefix, nested mounts are legal, and payload images stay read-only (writes fail EROFS).</text>
          <text x="470" y="444" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">the pair check (3) runs post-mount, before any payload or interpreter touch — spec 18 C3</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ THE HANDOFF, IN PROSE ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">The handoff, stated exactly.</h2>
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        <p>
          Whoever launches the runtime — the bootstrap of a stitched package, the shim in
          managed mode, or <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">tebako run</code> —
          exports{' '}
          <code class="rounded bg-[var(--tb-c-divider)] px-1.5 py-0.5 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">TEBAKO_RUNTIME_IMAGE=&lt;absolute path of the cached .tfs&gt;</code>
          {' '}and execs the interpreter. The driver mounts that image <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">whole
          at the runtime root as the first mount</strong>, then the payload triples in argv order
          (the image-era env var is a bare path mounted whole — the{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">-</code> semantics without a triple).
          On the standalone path the trailer's runtime reference carries the bare{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">;image</code> flag that tells the loader
          to resolve and verify the image alongside the executable (spec 05 §1, spec 06 §2).
        </p>
        <p>
          Generations meet fail-closed. A driver that implements spec 17's grammar declares{' '}
          <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">contract version 2</strong> — compiled in as{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">TEBAKO_CONTRACT_VERSION</code> and
          declared in the release manifest, and the two must agree. The loader negotiates
          <em> before any checksum acceptance</em>: an unsupported contract is exit{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">75</code>, naming both generations and
          the remedy — upgrade tebako, or pin an older runtime — never a silent accept.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ THE MOUNT ROOT HAS ONE OWNER ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">The mount root has one owner.</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 max-w-3xl text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        The runtime root — ruby: <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">/__tfs__</code> on
        POSIX, <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">A:/t</code> on windows, short by
        owner decision for MAX_PATH headroom — is a contract value, so it has exactly one
        authoritative source: the patch literals in{' '}
        <a href={LINKS.rubyRepo} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">tamatebako/ruby</a>.
        Everything downstream <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">flows</strong> it; nothing
        re-authors it (the SSOT invariant):
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 940 300" class="w-full min-w-[760px]" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Mount-root flow: tamatebako/ruby patch literals, source tarball tebako-mount-root manifest, runtime factory, interpreter exe and env image layout.yaml pair, driver verification with exit 78 on mismatch">
          <defs>
            <marker id="rf-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <g transform="translate(20, 40)">
            <rect width="170" height="88" rx="10" fill="var(--color-ink)" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="85" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-mist-pale)">tamatebako/ruby</text>
            <text x="85" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--color-gold)">patch literals — THE OWNER</text>
            <text x="85" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--color-mist)" opacity="0.85">the only hand-written copy</text>
          </g>
          <line x1="196" y1="84" x2="216" y2="84" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#rf-arrow)" />

          <g transform="translate(222, 40)">
            <rect width="170" height="88" rx="10" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="85" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-1)">source tarball</text>
            <text x="85" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">tebako-mount-root manifest</text>
            <text x="85" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">C1 · absent/corrupt → exit 132</text>
          </g>
          <line x1="398" y1="84" x2="418" y2="84" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#rf-arrow)" />

          <g transform="translate(424, 40)">
            <rect width="170" height="88" rx="10" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="85" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-1)">runtime factory</text>
            <text x="85" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">flows it — never re-authors</text>
            <text x="85" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="9" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">C2 · release card carries it</text>
          </g>
          <line x1="600" y1="84" x2="620" y2="84" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#rf-arrow)" />

          <g transform="translate(626, 14)">
            <rect width="140" height="60" rx="10" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="70" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-1)">the exe</text>
            <text x="70" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">compiled-in root (entry TU)</text>
            <rect y="76" width="140" height="60" rx="10" fill="var(--tb-c-card)" stroke="var(--tb-c-divider-strong)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="70" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="11.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--tb-c-text-1)">the env image</text>
            <text x="70" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">/lib/tebako/layout.yaml</text>
            <text x="70" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">C3 · one factory pair</text>
          </g>
          <line x1="772" y1="84" x2="792" y2="84" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#rf-arrow)" />

          <g transform="translate(798, 40)">
            <rect width="122" height="88" rx="10" fill="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke="var(--tb-c-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="61" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-display), sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-paper)">the driver</text>
            <text x="61" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--color-paper)" opacity="0.92">compares post-mount,</text>
            <text x="61" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--color-paper)" opacity="0.92">before ruby init</text>
            <text x="61" y="78" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--color-paper)" opacity="0.92">mismatch → exit 78</text>
          </g>

          <text x="470" y="220" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">A mismatched pair is refused with both values printed — never a ruby LoadError from a half-right mount.</text>
          <text x="470" y="240" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans), sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">On windows the driver qualifies every declared mount onto the root's drive — the wire grammar never carries one.</text>
          <text x="470" y="272" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono), monospace" font-size="10" fill="var(--tb-c-text-3)">the in-image declaration grammar: docs/spec/schemas/layout.yaml — owned there, mirrored by crates/tebako-driver</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        The exe's compiled-in root and the image's declared{' '}
        <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">mount_root</code> (in{' '}
        <a href={LINKS.layoutSchema} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">/lib/tebako/layout.yaml</a>)
        are two flowings of the same literal, built as one pair. The driver checks them against
        each other on every boot: that is what makes a stale or mismatched pairing a named
        refusal instead of a broken load path.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h2>Moving the root: <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)]">TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT</code>.</h2>
        <StatusPill status="shipped" note="spec 17 §1 — locked 2026-08-08" />
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        <p>
          The baked root is the per-platform <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">default, not
          the only spelling</strong>. Set <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT</code>
          {' '}in the runtime's environment and the driver mounts the env image at that root
          instead — and everything downstream follows: era-2 rbconfig emits{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">ENV["TEBAKO_MOUNT_ROOT"] || &lt;baked&gt;</code>,
          the io-routing patches read the driver-reported root, and declared payload mounts
          qualify onto the override's drive exactly as they do the baked root's.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two gates keep the override honest, in order:
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">GATE 1 · FORM — BEFORE ANY MOUNT</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The value must be an absolute path (<code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">/…</code>
            {' '}or drive-qualified <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">X:/…</code>) with no
            trailing slash and no <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">..</code>. A malformed
            value is <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">exit 65, naming the variable</strong> —
            before anything mounts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
          <p class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">GATE 2 · GRANT — POST-MOUNT</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
            The image must declare <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs">mount_root_override: true</code>
            {' '}(layout schema_minor 1). An image without the grant predates the override era — its
            rbconfig is pinned to the baked root — so the driver refuses with{' '}
            <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">exit 78, naming both the override and the
            image</strong>. Never a boot whose load paths point at an unmounted root.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ THE CACHE ENTRY ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">The cache entry.</h2>
      <p class="mb-6 max-w-2xl text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        Under <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">~/.tebako</code>, a runtime entry holds
        immutable artifacts and their trusted markers — nothing else (spec 05 §3):
      </p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)] sm:text-sm" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);"><code>runtimes/&lt;lang&gt;-&lt;lv&gt;-&lt;ver&gt;-&lt;triplet&gt;/
  tebako-runtime-&lt;ver&gt;-&lt;lv&gt;-&lt;triplet&gt;[.exe]   # interpreter (0755)
  sha256 / origin                             # executable markers
  tebako-runtime-&lt;ver&gt;-&lt;lv&gt;-&lt;triplet&gt;.tfs     # env image (0444)
  &lt;image&gt;.sha256                              # trust anchor: "&lt;sha&gt;  &lt;file&gt;\n"
  &lt;image&gt;.origin                              # the URL it was fetched from</code></pre>
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        <p>
          The <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">.sha256</code> marker <em>is</em> the
          trust anchor: its presence means the artifact was sha256-verified at install; it is
          re-verified only when re-fetched, <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">never per
          run</strong>. Installs are tmp + rename under a per-entry flock — a partial install is
          invisible — and a checksum mismatch on download deletes the download and leaves the
          cache untouched (spec 05 §4–§5).
        </p>
        <p>
          The one place extraction still exists is <em>press time</em>, and it is not a cache
          shape: when the packager needs the runtime's files as a build environment, it extracts
          the cached image in-process through the TFS ABI into the build prefix — rebuilt per
          press, never stored back. The run side mounts; it never extracts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ WHY .tfs ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-3">Why <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)]">.tfs</code> and not <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)]">.dwarfs</code>.</h2>
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
        <p>
          The env image's metadata is serialized with <strong class="text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">FlatBuffers</strong>
          {' '}— the dwarfs-t writer's default in our builds — which upstream DwarFS cannot read.
          A format upstream can't open doesn't get upstream's extension:{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">.tfs</code> marks a TFS image
          (content-detected by the reader regardless of extension), while{' '}
          <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">.dwarfs</code> stays reserved for
          upstream-compatible images. The writer binding lives in{' '}
          <a href={LINKS.dwarfsTRs} class="tb-link-underline font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">dwarfs-t-rs</a>
          {' '}— image creation is in-process, never a shelled mkdwarfs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Format is orthogonal to role: the extension and the <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">format_id</code>
          {' '}answer exactly one question — how to read these bytes. Payloads pressed today
          default to the limnifs format (spec 20, since CLI v0.2.0); the runtime factory's env
          images are dwarfs-t-native. Both are <code class="font-[var(--font-mono)] text-sm">.tfs</code>,
          and the runtime contract on this page doesn't change either way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ STATED PLAINLY ============ -->
    <div class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="mb-6">Stated plainly.</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)]" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[640px] text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--tb-c-divider-strong)] font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-3)]">
              <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">SITUATION</th>
              <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--tb-c-divider)]">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">boot without TEBAKO_RUNTIME_IMAGE</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">A legal shape — a bare interpreter — but the driver names the absence on stderr (stdout belongs to the payload). In managed mode a missing handoff is a launcher bug, surfaced loudly — not a silent fallback onto an embedded copy.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">exe from one build, image from another</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">Refused by name: the pair check compares the image's declared mount_root against the exe's compiled-in value post-mount, before the interpreter inits — exit 78 with both values printed. Never a ruby LoadError.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">writes into a mounted image</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">EROFS. Payload and env images are read-only forever; write and encryption overlays live only in the Rust TFS layer, and dwarfs-t never learns to write (the transforms law).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-[var(--font-mono)] text-xs text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)]">windows today</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">The handoff is shipped on macOS and Linux; the windows exec and locking port is partial (spec 06 status, roadmap 02). The contract itself — roots, overrides, exit codes — is platform-uniform by design.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

